From: Michael Narine <michael@verita-ai.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 18:15:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PrintObject: initialise m_id to zero

PrintObject::m_id (the object's index in the print) is never initialised. It is assigned
only by the exclude-object code in GCode.cpp and by the CLI/GUI, but the
"; printing object NAME id:N copy K" comment that gcode_label_objects emits reads it
unconditionally. Any other caller prints an indeterminate value (found by the Slicewright
cube test: id:7018616065285169712 instead of id:0).

Value-initialise it to zero at its declaration.

Purpose: Fix an uninitialised member: PrintObject::m_id is printed in the object label comment but only assigned by some callers.
SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
Upstream-Status: to be submitted
Orca-Base: v2.4.2
---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
--- a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
@@ -579,7 +579,7 @@
     // SoftFever
     // 
     // object id
-    size_t               m_id;
+    size_t               m_id = 0;
     void apply_conical_overhang();
 
  public:
